  "releaseNotes": "v.1.8.0\n\t\t\t- Added UseWatch option to run the external project with 'dotnet watch' (recompile/hot reload on change)\n\t\t\t- Debug and Git Pull now work while an external project runs under watch\n\t\t\t- Raised minimum Aspire to 13.5\n\t\t\tv.1.7.0\n\t\t\t- Show the launch profile's launchUrl in the dashboard\n\t\t\tv.1.6.0\n\t\t\t- Updated to target .NET 10\n\t\t\t- Raised minimum Aspire to 13.4\n\t\t\t- Honor ExcludeLaunchProfile to make launchSettings.json optional\n\t\t\t- Show the 'Git Pull' output in the dashboard\n\t\t\tv.1.5.0\n\t\t\t- Updated to latest Aspire 13\n\t\t\tv.1.4.0\n\t\t\t- Updated to latest Aspire 9.3.1\n\t\t\tv.1.3.0\n\t\t\t- Added option to set the debugger launch command + arguments\n\t\t\tv.1.2.1\n\t\t\t- Fixed issue with launch profile not being set correctly\n\t\t\t- Correctly adding the command line arguments to the external project on startup\n\t\t\tv.1.2.0\n\t\t\t- Updated to Aspire 9.1.0\n\t\t\t- Added SolutionGroup property in the settings for startup-avoidance\n\t\t\tv.1.1.0\n\t\t\t- Improved pid retrieval and added option to launch a debugger from inside the external project\n\t\t\tv.1.0.0\n\t\t\t- First release",
